KZ2 patch 6049 (ENHANCEMENT): motion mode for the SIXAXIS words; patch 4015's L1+R1 stick stand-in is removed.

Killzone 2 turns valves and arms demolition charges by tilting the pad. Patch 4015 tilted the motion words from the
right stick X while L1+R1 were held on a pad without sensors (36 deg at full stick). Root cause of the reports that it
"does not fully work" and soft-locks in the second mission: the charge arms only while the hand is inside its
ArmRanges windows (33.38..37.31 deg, 0x001174A8), and the hand follows the tilt with a 1 deg dead band (the
controllers' constructors, 0x00107700 / 0x00108C90), so 4015's map armed only with the stick at 95.6..100 % of its
travel; a pad, mapper or driver that stops a few per cent short never arms. A second cause: 4015 switched itself off
for any pad that reported a sensor, including a gyro-only or a 0 g virtual pad.
The port now feeds the stick to the game's two tilt readers directly (port/kz2/kz2_motion.h and the hook on the motion
getter 0x000821D0 in port/kz2/kz2_ppu_overrides.cpp; the tilt reaches the middle of the windows from 57 % of the stick).
This patch keeps cellPad's side small:
- pad_motion_stick.h (rewritten): the words by mode (auto/on: the pad's accelerometer once it has read gravity, else a
  still DS3; off: a still DS3) and the gravity latch; pad_host.h gets has_accel (set by pad_sdl_sensors).
- cellPad.c: pad_motion_set_mode() (the title port sets gameplay.ini's motion = auto|on|off), pad_motion_port() (the
  latch and the last right stick X byte the game got, for the title port's hook), and one line per XInput slot when a
  pad is reached over XInput, which has no motion sensors, with what the valves and charges will do.
KZ2_MOTION_STICK=0 (4015's switch) is read by the title port as motion = on.

